NV_PK(2,{"one of the hard white parts inside the body of a fish or animal":"","be careful this fish has a lot of bones":"","belly":"","the soft front part of the body below the chest":"","fish farm":"","a place often a pond where people raise fish to sell":"","my uncle runs a fish farm near the sea":"","congee":"","rice cooked in a lot of water until it becomes soft and thick":"","i'd like a bowl of hot congee please":"","in the 1940s a cook named hsu liu yi at tainan's sakariba market today's kangle market borrowed an idea from western cooking he deep fried a thick slice of toast cut off the top as a lid hollowed out the middle and filled it with chicken chicken liver seafood vegetables and a thick creamy sauce he first called it chicken liver board":"","the best known story says a university professor looked at the square fried box with its lid open and joked that it looked like a coffin the owner liked the joke and renamed it coffin board the scary name made it unforgettable and it became famous all over taiwan":"","today there are seafood curry and chicken versions and even dessert ones dip the lid into the filling first then scoop up the rest with a spoon":"","sakariba comes from a japanese word meaning a lively bustling place":"","it looks like a coffin but it tastes like a treasure box":"","dip the lid into the sauce first":"","the name sounds scary but the food is delicious":""});